<title>SPAIN: Spain's Inespal could be sold soon - SEPI.</title>
<headline>Spain's Inespal could be sold soon - SEPI.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish aluminium firm Inespal could be privatised in the next few months, state holding company SEPI said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Sources in SEPI said that talks with unidentified foreign company could end quite soon, adding that approval from the Spanish government was necessary to finalise the sale.</p>
<p>Local press reports in mid-January said the Industry Ministry had reopened talks with U.S. group Alcoa for the possible sale of the aluminium producer.</p>
<p>Other foreign groups were also tipped to have interest in Inespal, including Canada's Alcan, Dutch group Hoogovens NV, Norway's Hydroa Aluminium and Swiss group Glencore.</p>
<p>In 1995, Inespal's pre-tax profit rose to 15.67 billion pesetas but 1996 pre-tax profit was expected to fall to around 4.0 billion pesetas.</p>
<p>-- Madrid Newsroom, + 341 585 8340</p>
</text>
